.TH SKYBOX-THUMBS-REMOTE 1 "2026-10-25" "skybox-thumbs-remote" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
skybox-thumbs-remote \- run skybox-thumbs on the Proxmox host over SSH
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B skybox-thumbs-remote
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B skybox-thumbs-remote
is a thin wrapper that executes
.I /usr/local/bin/skybox-thumbs
on the Proxmox host, where the media share is mounted locally. All arguments
are passed through unchanged, so the options are those of
.BR skybox-thumbs (1).
.P
The SSH connection uses
.B BatchMode=yes
and disables the
.B RemoteCommand
and TTY settings normally applied by the host's
.I ~/.ssh/config
entry, so the wrapper works non-interactively.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SKYBOX_THUMBS_SERVER
SSH host alias to use. Default: \fIproxmox\fR.
.TP
.B SKYBOX_THUMBS_BIN
Remote executable path. Default: \fI/usr/local/bin/skybox-thumbs\fR.
.SH EXAMPLES
Generate thumbnails with the remote defaults:
.IP
.EX
skybox-thumbs-remote
.EE
.P
Pilot run and prune:
.IP
.EX
skybox-thumbs-remote \-\-limit 3
skybox-thumbs-remote \-\-prune
.EE
.SH EXIT STATUS
The exit status of the remote command, or the SSH client's status if the
connection fails.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR skybox-thumbs (1),
.BR ssh (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Written for local use.
